  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Rockeater Rocky is on a mission to eat rocks!\n\nThere are NNN rocks on the XXX-axis. The ithi^{th}ith of these rocks is at position XiX_iXi​ and has weight WiW_iWi​.\n\nAll the WiW_iWi​ are **distinct**.\n\nConsider a subset SSS consisting of kkk rocks. Rocky will eat the rocks in SSS as follows:\n\n\nLet i1,i2,…,iki_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_ki1​,i2​,…,ik​ be the list of indices of rocks in SSS, sorted in **ascending** order of weight.\n\nThat is, Wi1&lt;Wi2&lt;…&lt;WikW_{i_1} \\lt W_{i_2} \\lt \\ldots \\lt W_{i_k}Wi1​​&lt;Wi2​​&lt;…&lt;Wik​​\n\n\nRocky will eat the rocks in SSS in ascending order of weight. That is, Rocky will start at position Xi1X_{i_1}Xi1​​ and eat the rock there; then move to position Xi2X_{i_2}Xi2​​ and eat the rock there, and so on till all the rocks in SSS are eaten.\nThe distance traveled by Rocky is thus ∣Xi1−Xi2∣+∣Xi2−Xi3∣+…+∣Xik−1−Xik∣|X_{i_1} - X_{i_2}| + |X_{i_2} - X_{i_3}| + \\ldots + |X_{i_{k-1}} - X_{i_k}|∣Xi1​​−Xi2​​∣+∣Xi2​​−Xi3​​∣+…+∣Xik−1​​−Xik​​∣.\nIn particular, if ∣S∣≤1|S| \\leq 1∣S∣≤1 the distance traveled by Rocky is 000.\nRocky hasn't decided yet which subset of rocks to eat.\n\nIf every subset is equally likely to be chosen, find the **expected value** of the distance traveled by Rocky, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\nMore formally, under the constraints of the problem, it can be proved that the expected value can be represented as a rational number, i.e, an irreducible fraction PQ\\frac{P}{Q}QP​​.\nFurther, there exists a unique integer RRR such that R×Q≡P(mod109+7)R\\times Q \\equiv P \\pmod {10^9 + 7}R×Q≡P(mod109+7) and 0≤R&lt;109+70\\leq R \\lt 10^9+70≤R&lt;109+7. Print this integer RRR.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of rocks.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers X1,X2,…,XNX_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_NX1​,X2​,…,XN​ — the positions of the rocks.\nThe third line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers W1,W2,…,WNW_1, W_2, \\ldots, W_NW1​,W2​,…,WN​ — the weights of the rocks.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the expected distance traveled by Rocky, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1041 \\leq T \\leq 3\\cdot 10^41≤T≤3⋅104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Wi≤N1 \\leq W_i \\leq N1≤Wi​≤N",
      "All the WiW_iWi​ are distinct",
      "1≤X1&lt;X2&lt;…&lt;XN≤1091 \\leq X_1 \\lt X_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt X_N \\leq 10^91≤X1​&lt;X2​&lt;…&lt;XN​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
