        "input": "3\n2\n1 5\n2 1\n3\n1 20 34\n1 3 2\n6\n23 54 56 85 109 126\n6 3 2 5 1 4",
        "output": "1\n125000015\n312500100",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There are four possible subsets Rocky can choose. Three of them ({},{1},{5}\\{\\}, \\{1\\}, \\{5\\}{},{1},{5}) require no travel, while in the fourth ({1,5})(\\{1, 5\\})({1,5}), Rocky has to travel a distance of ∣5−1∣=4|5 - 1| = 4∣5−1∣=4.\nThe expected distance traveled is hence the average of 0+0+0+40 + 0 + 0 + 40+0+0+4, which is 111.\nTest case 222: There are 888 possible subsets of rocks. Four of them have a travel distance of 000. For the rest:\n\n{1,20}\\{1, 20\\}{1,20} has a travel distance of 191919.\n{1,34}\\{1, 34\\}{1,34} has a travel distance of 333333.\n{20,34}\\{20, 34\\}{20,34} has a travel distance of 141414.\n{1,20,34}\\{1, 20, 34\\}{1,20,34} has a travel distance of 474747, because Rocky moves 1→34→201 \\to 34 \\to 201→34→20 in ascending order of rock weights.\n\nThe answer is thus the average of 0+0+0+0+19+14+33+47=1130 + 0 + 0 + 0 + 19 + 14 + 33 + 47 = 1130+0+0+0+19+14+33+47=113, and 1138\\frac{113}{8}8113​ modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7 is 125000015125000015125000015."
      }
